    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lacunar stroke about three and a half months ago (I69.354)</content>. Modified Rankin Scale 1: back to full work with only mild left hand fatigue. Mood screen in the remission range (PHQ-9 4). [S]<list><item>Continue clopidogrel and atorvastatin long term.</item><item>For the speech: rest beforehand, keep to water while speaking, and take a break if the hand or speech tires.</item><item>MoCA at the annual wellness visit later this month.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension (I10)</content>. 126/74 mmHg seated without orthostatic fall. [S]<list><item>No change; basic metabolic panel in January.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, cigars (F17.290)</content>. Three cigars a day, his agreed goal; not ready to stop. [S]<list><item>Advice to stop repeated.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure seated and standing, weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seated 126/74 mmHg, standing 122/72 mmHg; weight 78.6 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Modified Rankin Scale</td><td>At 90 days and at follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>1 at about fifteen weeks, the scheduled review nearest to 90 days</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>First post-stroke visit, then periodically while symptoms persist; at least yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4, in the remission range; item 9 scored 0; next at least yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antithrombotic and statin adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking clopidogrel and atorvastatin; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting or changing a statin, then every 3 to 12 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL cholesterol 58 mg/dL in August; next within a year</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel</td><td>Every 6 months on an ACE inhibitor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Last at the end of July; due in January</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; gait normal</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical and occupational therapy</td><td>Through recovery; reassess on plateau or worsening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Discharged two weeks ago with goals met</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Alcohol use (AUDIT-C)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Up to date</td><td>5 in August; repeat at the wellness visit; drinking reviewed today and advice repeated</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three cigars a day; advice to stop</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Obstructive sleep apnea evaluation</td><td>Consider for all after stroke</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Asked again: no snoring, witnessed apneas, or new daytime sleepiness; sleep testing still declined</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>Again within the first year</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit later this month</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Influenza vaccination</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit later this month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Lower blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg without orthostatic symptoms by the eight-week review. Outcome by 2026-08-19: Blood pressure 128/76 mmHg on amlodipine 5 mg and lisinopril 5 mg; no orthostatic fall [S]</item><item>Lower LDL cholesterol below 70 mg/dL by the eight-week review. Outcome by 2026-08-19: LDL cholesterol 58 mg/dL on atorvastatin 80 mg [S]</item><item>Return to full work and public speaking by about three months after the stroke. Outcome by 2026-10-07: Back at full work; modified Rankin Scale 1 [S]</item><item>Keep to no more than two drinks on any day. Outcome by 2026-10-07: AUDIT-C from 8 to 5; no longer drinking six or more on one occasion, but still above two drinks on some days [S]</item><item>Cut down to three cigars a day as a step toward stopping. Outcome by 2026-10-07: Three cigars a day; not ready to stop [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); Primary Care of Adult Patients After Stroke: A Scientific Statement From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, stroke/TIA, hypertension, and depression monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit later this month. Stroke and blood pressure review in about three months. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-28: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

